# ── Relatum-distinctness assertions (a relator's two roles must bind distinct values) ──
# The canonical carrier for a mutual-inequality integrity condition on a relator: two
# named roles on one focus node must bind DISTINCT values. OWL functionality of each role
# does not reject a coincidence (it infers OWL sameAs); the native coherence gate joins
# logic:distinctnessTarget + the two logic:distinctnessRole values to raise a violation
# when they coincide, and the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection.
# This slice owns the vocabulary; every record whose logic:distinctnessTarget is a term of a
# non-grounding slice is authored in THAT slice's module.ttl (the tier rule, docs/GROUNDING.md).

logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion
    a logic:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "relatum distinctness assertion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A central record asserting that, on a target class, two named roles must bind DISTINCT values on any one focus node — the mutual-inequality integrity condition of a relator whose relata must differ (a Commitment's committed agent and beneficiary, a Criterion's reward and penalty poles). It names the class with logic:distinctnessTarget and the two roles with logic:distinctnessRole, the triple the native coherence gate joins to raise a violation when the roles coincide, and carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes. The reasoning authority names and enforces it here; the domain slice keeps the OWL-facing role declarations. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:distinctnessTarget
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "distinctness target"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains (the relator class). Read together with logic:distinctnessRole, it tells the native coherence gate which class bears the mutual-inequality condition. Domain logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion; single-valued. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:distinctnessRole
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "distinctness role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion to one of the two roles that must bind distinct values on a focus node. Exactly two are asserted per record; the native coherence gate raises a violation when both roles bind the same value on one focus node. Domain logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion; two-valued. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

# ── Key / uniqueness assertions (a class is identified by a key property) ─────────────
# The canonical carrier for a KEY integrity condition: on a target class, the value of one key
# property uniquely picks out the instance — two instances agreeing on the key value are the same
# individual, and two asserted distinct yet agreeing are a contradiction. It is the logic: analogue
# of an OWL 2 DL OWL hasKey axiom, minted standalone so a datatype/single-property key survives as a
# native reasoning carrier rather than a source OWL hasKey triple. The native DL consistency gate
# joins logic:keyClass + logic:keyProperty to decide the key-agreement clash; the OWL OWL hasKey
# axiom is its lossy DL view and the derived inverse sh:maxCount 1 its SHACL projection.
# This slice owns the vocabulary; every record whose logic:keyClass is a term of a non-grounding
# slice is authored in THAT slice's module.ttl (the tier rule, docs/GROUNDING.md).

logic:KeyAssertion
    a logic:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "key assertion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A central record asserting that a class is identified by a KEY: the value of a single key property uniquely picks out the class instance, so two instances agreeing on the key value are the same individual — and two asserted distinct yet agreeing are a contradiction. It names the class with logic:keyClass and the key property with logic:keyProperty, the pair the native DL consistency gate joins to decide the key-agreement clash, and carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes. This is the canonical logic: carrier of a datatype/single-property key: minted standalone (the logic: analogue of an OWL 2 DL OWL hasKey axiom, which on a datatype property is the DL-safe alternative to an OWL 2 Full OWL InverseFunctionalProperty), so the key is a native reasoning obligation rather than a source OWL hasKey triple. The reasoning authority names and enforces it here; the OWL OWL hasKey axiom is its lossy DL view and the derived inverse sh:maxCount 1 its SHACL projection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:keyClass
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:KeyAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "key class"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:KeyAssertion to the class its key identifies — the class whose instances the key value uniquely picks out. Read together with logic:keyProperty, it tells the native DL consistency gate which class bears the key: two instances of this class agreeing on every key value are the same individual. Domain logic:KeyAssertion; single-valued. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

logic:keyProperty
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain logic:KeyAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "key property"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:KeyAssertion to the property whose value keys the class — the single key property whose value uniquely identifies a logic:keyClass instance. Co-present with logic:keyClass: a key assertion carrying one without the other names no enforceable key. A record naming several logic:keyProperty values states a COMPOSITE key (the tuple of values is unique, not each part), which has no single-path uniqueness shape; the seeded keys are single-property. Domain logic:KeyAssertion; single-valued for a single-property key."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce this record's integrity condition over instance; the record is the canonical carrier the gate joins."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when instance no longer bears the condition — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read the record's own logic: fields together: they name instance and the condition asserted over it, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching axiom from them."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about instance and nothing else. It is not a definition of instance (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "logic:keyProperty logic:characterizes instance ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .
# ── Conditional-range assertions (a discriminant value fixes a relatum's type) ────────
# The canonical carrier for a value-conditioned range integrity condition on a relator: on
# a target class, a discriminant property bound to a NAMED value forces the value bound by a
# second property to be an instance of a required type. OWL cannot state a value-conditioned
# range without nominals it deliberately keeps out of the DL profile; the native coherence
# gate joins logic:conditionalRangeTarget + selector/value + required type to raise a
# violation when the discriminant matches but the required type is absent, and the generated
# SHACL constraint surface is its projection. This slice owns the vocabulary; every record whose
# logic:conditionalRangeTarget is a term of a non-grounding slice is authored in THAT slice's
# module.ttl (the tier rule, docs/GROUNDING.md).

logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion
    a logic:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "conditional range assertion"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A central record asserting that, on a target class, a focus node whose gmeow:-selector property carries a NAMED value must bind — through a second value property — an instance of a required type. It names the class with logic:conditionalRangeTarget, the discriminant property with logic:conditionalRangeSelector and its triggering value with logic:conditionalRangeSelectorValue, the constrained property with logic:conditionalRangeValue, and the demanded type with logic:conditionalRangeRequiredType; the native coherence gate joins them to raise a violation when the selector matches yet the value is not of the required type. Carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

logic:conditionalRangeTarget
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
