    skos:definition "The formalization candidate that harvests the pairwise disjointness of the four kernel top sortals from gmeow:PhysicalObject's gmeow:avoidWhen prose (which states the three others are disjoint with PhysicalObject by design) into the enforced OWL disjointWith integrity constraints asserted in the kernel: gmeow:Agent, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:InformationObject and gmeow:SocialObject are pairwise disjoint EXCEPT the deliberately-preserved SocialObject∩InformationObject overlap. The gmeow:Agent ⊥ gmeow:SocialObject edge is net-new on this branch. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqTopSortalDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqTopSortalDisjointClashRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:PhysicalObject, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:avoidWhen text so a later edit surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the OWL disjointWith directly, forcing a two-sortal individual to OWL Nothing."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:candidateSourceHash "sha256:82ff1dac761cc77e2acb02a0a81e079ba64bebc2337f4e190489a9c074b1af35"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateExtractionProvenance "hand-harvested from the gmeow:PhysicalObject gmeow:avoidWhen annotation, which states the three other sortals are disjoint with PhysicalObject by design (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateScope "pairwise OWL disjointWith among the four top sortals gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject and gmeow:SocialObject, except the preserved gmeow:SocialObject ∩ gmeow:InformationObject overlap"^^xsd:string ;
