    skos:definition "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing logic:licensedFalsehoodNotDeception: a gmeow:Event whose projected standpoint is gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood is excluded from gmeow:eventTypeDeception — the fiction/satire/sarcasm safety property that separates harmless non-truth-asserting frames from deception. Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (strong negation), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood's skos:definition. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqLicensedFalsehoodSafeHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqLicensedFalsehoodDeceptionRejected)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:candidateSourceHash "sha256:885472a556e60956181fc7f7e512fbee34b63d02349fb8ca1388f2736fdf6589"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateExtractionProvenance "hand-harvested from gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood's skos:definition, which states the licensed-falsehood safety property separates fiction/satire/sarcasm from deception (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)"^^xsd:string ;
