    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "bullshit as truth-indifference holds"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the bullshit-modality equivalence must satisfy: a gmeow:StandpointClaim whose gmeow:claimModality is gmeow:bullshit is exactly one whose gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness is gmeow:truthIndifferent (Frankfurt) — held without regard for correspondence, distinct from a lie's truth-aimed denial. The well-formed case the biconditional admits."@x-gmeow-english .
logic:cqBullshitIndifferenceLieRejected
    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "bullshit conflated with lying is rejected"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative countermodel the bullshit-modality equivalence must respect: conflating gmeow:bullshit with a truth-aimed lie (gmeow:truthAimed) is rejected — bullshit is indifferent to truth, a lie asserts against a believed truth. HONEST SCOPE: the equivalence is realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection; the native monotone chase does not enforce a biconditional, disclosed in the loss ledger."@x-gmeow-english .
