# ── Diagnostics gate: the fatal verdict as the principal up-set of the truth order
# (severity=Error) ∧ (category→Blocking) ∧ (standpoint=Binding) ⇒
#   gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal.
# The RDF-side derivation of the single Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() policy
# morphism: a meet of three monotone axis-maps whose Fatal region is exactly the
# principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding). The rule joins a finding's severity,
# its category's gmeow:categoryBlocking projection (asserted in the diagnostics
# slice), and its standpoint. Because Fatal is reachable only from the top of all
# three axes, an advisory-standpoint or Coherent-category finding can never be
# derived Fatal — the two never-gate theorems fall out of the construction, not a
# special case. The diagnostics conformance lane proves the derived Fatal set
# equals gate()'s over every grade.

logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict
    a logic:Rule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "derive the fatal gate verdict on the principal up-set of the truth ordering"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits gmeow:findingGateVerdict(finding, gmeow:gateFatal) whenever a finding's gmeow:findingSeverity is gmeow:severityError, its gmeow:findingCategory's gmeow:categoryBlocking projection is gmeow:blockingBlocking, and its gmeow:findingStandpoint is gmeow:standpointBinding: the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding) of the truth ordering, the meet of three monotone axis-maps. The RDF-side derivation of the single Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() policy morphism. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Because Fatal is reachable only from the top of all three axes, an advisory-standpoint or Coherent-category finding is structurally unable to be derived Fatal — the two never-gate theorems fall out of the up-set construction, not a special case."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:findingGateVerdict ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingGateVerdict ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:gateFatal
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingSeverity ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:severityError
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingCategory ;
        rdf:object    "?category"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?category" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:categoryBlocking ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:blockingBlocking
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingStandpoint ;
        rdf:object    gmeow:standpointBinding
    ] .

logic:cqGateFatalVerdictHolds
    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "the fatal verdict is derived on the top of all three truth axes"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the gate rule must satisfy: given a finding with gmeow:findingSeverity gmeow:severityError, a gmeow:findingCategory whose gmeow:categoryBlocking is gmeow:blockingBlocking (a failure kind), and gmeow:findingStandpoint gmeow:standpointBinding, the reasoner must derive gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal — the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding) the harvested prose commits to, agreeing with Rust gate() returning Fatal."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected
    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "an advisory-standpoint finding is never derived fatal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The first never-gate countermodel the gate rule must respect: a finding whose gmeow:findingStandpoint is gmeow:standpointAdvisory is NEVER derived gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, no matter how loud its severity or how blocking its category — the standpoint axis is below the Binding top, so the meet cannot reach Fatal. The boundary that keeps advice from ever failing the gate, mirroring Rust gate() returning Collected for every advisory grade."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected
    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "a permitted-epistemic-conflict finding is never derived fatal"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The second never-gate countermodel the gate rule must respect: a finding whose gmeow:findingCategory is logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict — whose gmeow:categoryBlocking projection is gmeow:blockingCoherent — is NEVER derived gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, even at gmeow:severityError and gmeow:standpointBinding, because its Blocking axis is below the Blocking top. The load-bearing boundary that a disclosed, coherent contradiction a glut-admitting contract permits does not fail the gate, mirroring Rust gate() returning Collected for every Coherent-category grade."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:candidateGateFatalVerdict
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "the fatal gate verdict derives on the principal up-set of the truth ordering"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict: it harvests the up-set construction documented in gmeow:findingGateVerdict's skos:definition (the verdict is gmeow:gateFatal exactly on the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding), the meet of the severity, blocking-projected category, and standpoint axes) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation — the RDF-side image of the single Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() policy morphism. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqGateFatalVerdictHolds) and two never-gate countermodels (logic:cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected, logic:cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingGateVerdict, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:candidateSourceHash "sha256:e12a391fb8dfadd6f26028567308db254ed169b158f4320f05e527c59b376359"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateExtractionProvenance "hand-harvested from gmeow:findingGateVerdict's skos:definition, which states the verdict is derived on exactly the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding) of the truth ordering, mirroring the Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() morphism (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateScope "derivation: (gmeow:findingSeverity gmeow:severityError) ∧ (gmeow:findingCategory ∘ gmeow:categoryBlocking gmeow:blockingBlocking) ∧ (gmeow:findingStandpoint gmeow:standpointBinding) ⇒ gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateContract logic:PositiveHornProfile ;
    logic:candidateCategory logic:CategoryDerivationRule ;
    logic:candidateLifecycle logic:CandidateAccepted ;
    logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation ;
    logic:candidatePositiveCase logic:cqGateFatalVerdictHolds ;
    logic:candidateNegativeCase logic:cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected ,
        logic:cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected ;
    logic:candidateProjectionBehavior logic:ExactPreservation ;
    logic:candidateSemanticRisk logic:RiskCoreContaminating ;
    logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingGateVerdict ;
    logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition .

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Diagnostic meta-reasoning — findings ABOUT findings over the projected graph.
#
# Every rule below is a gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule (subClassOf logic:Rule): the
# carrier-compose reasoner discovers each by TYPE and runs it over the projected
# diagnostic graph, so a new meta-finding is added by authoring a new tagged rule
# with zero engine change (design-decision-2's class selection). The fold derives
# the root-cause / cluster / cross-node-glut meta-findings whose schema lives in
# the diagnostics slice. Root-cause uses negation-as-failure (a childless root is
# a finding NOT in the derived gmeow:findingHasAntecedent set), so its rule is
# logic:StratifiedNAFProfile; the transitive-closure, cluster, glut, and
# root-finding rules are positive Horn. Fresh witness-node minting is not
# expressible in the reified-Horn chase, so the cross-node glut is carried as the
# derived gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith edge (Supported-polarity → Opposed-polarity).

# ── Root-cause step 1/2: the transitive closure of gmeow:findingAntecedent ──────
logic:ruleFindingTracesBase
    a logic:Rule ,
        gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "base case: a finding traces to its direct antecedent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits gmeow:findingTraces(finding, antecedent) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent an antecedent: the base case of the transitive closure of the witness-DAG derivation edge. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Paired with logic:ruleFindingTracesStep, which closes it recursively up the chain."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleFindingTracesBase ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:findingTraces ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingTraces ;
        rdf:object    "?antecedent"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingAntecedent ;
        rdf:object    "?antecedent"
    ] .

# ── Root-cause step 2/2: the recursive step of the closure ──────────────────────
logic:ruleFindingTracesStep
    a logic:Rule ,
        gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "recursive step: a finding traces to its antecedent's antecedents"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits gmeow:findingTraces(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent an intermediate finding that gmeow:findingTraces the root: the recursive step that closes gmeow:findingTraces transitively up the witness DAG. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone recursion the native chase settles to fixpoint; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Paired with logic:ruleFindingTracesBase."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleFindingTracesStep ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:findingTraces ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingTraces ;
        rdf:object    "?root"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingAntecedent ;
        rdf:object    "?intermediate"
    ] , [
        rdf:subject   "?intermediate" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingTraces ;
        rdf:object    "?root"
    ] .

logic:cqFindingTracesHolds
    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "a finding traces to every antecedent up its chain"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the transitive-closure rules must satisfy — 'every antecedent this finding derives from, directly or transitively': given F4 gmeow:findingAntecedent F2 and F2 gmeow:findingAntecedent F1, the reasoner must derive BOTH gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F2) and gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F1), closing the witness DAG up past the intermediate."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected
    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "a finding never traces to an unconnected finding"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative countermodel the transitive-closure rules must respect: gmeow:findingTraces is exactly the reachability closure of gmeow:findingAntecedent — a finding with no antecedent chain to another finding never traces to it, and the closure is directed (a root antecedent does not trace DOWN to its downstream witnesses). Two findings in disjoint witness DAGs share no gmeow:findingTraces edge."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:candidateFindingTraces
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "finding-traces is the transitive closure of the antecedent edge"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleFindingTracesBase and logic:ruleFindingTracesStep: it harvests the transitive-reachability commitment in gmeow:findingAntecedent's skos:definition (the reasoner joins UP the witness DAG, following the edge transitively to the root antecedent) into two enforced positive-Horn rules deriving the closure gmeow:findingTraces, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFindingTracesHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingAntecedent, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:candidateSourceHash "sha256:1c235478a61c8445e999099c51c2bbe90abc6d16b003a1c4defda617077e531f"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateExtractionProvenance "hand-harvested from gmeow:findingAntecedent's skos:definition, which states the reasoner can join up the witness DAG for root-cause analysis and a childless finding up the chain is a root antecedent (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateScope "derivation: gmeow:findingAntecedent ⇒ gmeow:findingTraces (base), and gmeow:findingAntecedent ∘ gmeow:findingTraces ⇒ gmeow:findingTraces (recursive step), the transitive closure up the witness DAG"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateContract logic:PositiveHornProfile ;
    logic:candidateCategory logic:CategoryDerivationRule ;
    logic:candidateLifecycle logic:CandidateAccepted ;
    logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation ;
    logic:candidatePositiveCase logic:cqFindingTracesHolds ;
    logic:candidateNegativeCase logic:cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected ;
    logic:candidateProjectionBehavior logic:ExactPreservation ;
    logic:candidateSemanticRisk logic:RiskCoreContaminating ;
    logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingAntecedent ;
    logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition .

# ── Root-cause helper: mark every finding that carries an antecedent ─────────────
logic:ruleFindingHasAntecedent
    a logic:Rule ,
        gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "mark a finding that has at least one antecedent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits the self-edge gmeow:findingHasAntecedent(finding, finding) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent anything: the positive one-place marker of a non-root finding, carried on a DEDICATED relation (not rdf:type). Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively. It exists so the stratified root-cause rule can express 'has no antecedent of its own' as a single negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent — the marker settles in a lower stratum than the NAF that reads it. Its own relation (rather than rdf:type) is load-bearing: negating rdf:type would form a negative cycle with the downstream rules that derive rdf:type from gmeow:findingRootCause, breaking stratification."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleFindingHasAntecedent ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:findingHasAntecedent ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingHasAntecedent ;
        rdf:object    "?finding"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingAntecedent ;
        rdf:object    "?antecedent"
    ] .

# ── Root cause: a traced antecedent that itself has no antecedent (NAF) ──────────
logic:ruleFindingRootCause
    a logic:Rule ,
        gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "derive a finding's root cause as a traced childless antecedent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Emits gmeow:findingRootCause(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingTraces a root that is NOT a gmeow:findingHasAntecedent of itself — i.e. the finding reaches the root up the witness DAG and the root has no antecedent of its own. The negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent makes this logic:StratifiedNAFProfile (the marker is derived in a lower stratum than this rule reads it); materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Honestly the shared ROOT antecedent, not a lowest-common-dominator: it names a childless root the finding derives from, without claiming uniqueness."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:provenance logic:ruleFindingRootCause ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:findingRootCause ;
    logic:head [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingRootCause ;
        rdf:object    "?root"
    ] ;
    logic:body [
        rdf:subject   "?finding" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingTraces ;
        rdf:object    "?root"
    ] ;
    logic:negatedBody [
        rdf:subject   "?root" ;
        rdf:predicate gmeow:findingHasAntecedent ;
        rdf:object    "?root"
    ] .

logic:cqFindingRootCauseHolds
    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "findings sharing one root all derive that childless root"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The positive competency case the root-cause rule must satisfy — 'the root of all findings sharing root R': given F2 and F3 that each gmeow:findingAntecedent the childless F1 (F1 has no antecedent), the reasoner must derive gmeow:findingRootCause(F2, F1) AND gmeow:findingRootCause(F3, F1), and transitively gmeow:findingRootCause(F4, F1) for an F4 that traces to F1 through F2 — the shared childless root, agreeing with the witness-DAG root-cause harvest."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:cqFindingRootCauseNonRootRejected
    a logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "an intermediate antecedent is never a root cause"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The negative countermodel the root-cause rule must respect: a traced antecedent that ITSELF carries a gmeow:findingAntecedent is never derived a gmeow:findingRootCause — only a childless root qualifies. For F4 → F2 → F1, F4's root cause is F1, NEVER the intermediate F2 (which is a gmeow:findingHasAntecedent of itself); and an independent finding with no antecedent chain derives no root cause at all. The boundary the negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent keeps."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:candidateFindingRootCause
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:FormalizationCandidate ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "a finding's root cause is a traced childless antecedent"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleFindingHasAntecedent and logic:ruleFindingRootCause: it harvests the root-cause commitment in gmeow:findingRootCause's skos:definition (the shared root antecedent reached by following gmeow:findingAntecedent transitively up the witness DAG to a childless witness, honestly the shared root and not a dominator) into an enforced stratified-negation rule set, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. The childless test is a negation-as-failure over the derived gmeow:findingHasAntecedent marker, so the contract is logic:StratifiedNAFProfile. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFindingRootCauseHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFindingRootCauseNonRootRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingRootCause, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:candidateSourceHash "sha256:0148fb862caa467b2cfbcea7d4fdd89b1841272bcf87ec188ee85b8654036b6f"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateExtractionProvenance "hand-harvested from gmeow:findingRootCause's skos:definition, which states the root is a childless witness reached by following gmeow:findingAntecedent transitively up the witness DAG, honestly the shared root antecedent and not a lowest-common-dominator (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)"^^xsd:string ;
    logic:candidateScope "derivation: gmeow:findingAntecedent ⇒ gmeow:findingHasAntecedent (self-edge), and gmeow:findingTraces to a root NOT gmeow:findingHasAntecedent of itself ⇒ gmeow:findingRootCause (stratified negation as failure)"^^xsd:string ;
