# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The self-describing existential-chase demonstrator.
#
# A minimal, genuine existential axiom that is TRUE of GMEOW's own reasoning:
# the native existential chase's OWN defining law — an existential obligation
# entails a Skolem witness. logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ⊑
# ∃logic:demonstratesChaseWitness.logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf is a narrow C ⊑ ∃p.D
# obligation; the two seeded demonstrand individuals inhabit C with NO asserted
# p-edge, so the native chase MUST invent one fresh Skolem witness (a
# gmeow:InventedWitness) per instance to discharge it — dogfooding the chase.
# D is a plain LEAF: not existential, disjointness-free, and never reaching C,
# so each invented null is inert (no Skolem ancestor-blocking cycle, no global
# inconsistency, weakly-acyclic and terminating).
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand
    a logic:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty logic:demonstratesChaseWitness ; logic:someValuesFrom logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf ] ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Existential Chase Demonstrand"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A narrow, self-describing existential obligation: a class each of whose instances carries the C ⊑ ∃p.D obligation `ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ⊑ ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf`, which the native existential chase MUST discharge by inventing a fresh Skolem witness (a gmeow:InventedWitness) for every instance that asserts no logic:demonstratesChaseWitness edge. It is deliberately narrow — ONLY the two seeded demonstrand individuals inhabit it — so the demonstration dogfoods the chase without cascading global inference over a widely-instantiated class. This is the native chase's own defining law made concrete and on-topic: an existential obligation entails a Skolem witness, and running the chase over this class is the minimal proof that GMEOW's own existential materializer actually fires."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid widening it (its whole point is that ONLY the two seeded demonstrand individuals inhabit it, so the invented nulls drive no cascading inference) and avoid adding an OWL disjointWith or a functional/cardinality axiom to it or its logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf — a demonstrand whose invented null is forced into a contradiction stops demonstrating the chase and starts breaking it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Seed at least two named individuals of this class with NO asserted logic:demonstratesChaseWitness edge and run the native existential chase; observe that it invents one distinct gmeow:InventedWitness (Skolem null) per instance to satisfy the ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf obligation, each recorded in the reasoned graph and its diagnostics projection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the minimal, self-describing demonstrator of the native existential chase — the on-topic C ⊑ ∃p.D obligation whose discharge mints the Skolem witnesses that dogfood GMEOW's own existential reasoning."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:demonstratesChaseWitness
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "demonstrates chase witness"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand to the logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf witness that discharges its existential obligation — the `p` in the demonstrator's C ⊑ ∃p.D law. Domain logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand, range logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf (stated in prose). When a demonstrand instance asserts no such edge, the native existential chase invents a fresh Skolem witness (a gmeow:InventedWitness) and materializes the demonstratesChaseWitness edge to it; the property is the object-property head `p` whose someValuesFrom obligation makes the chase fire — an object property, never a datatype property, so its value is an invented individual, not a literal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha logic:demonstratesChaseWitness <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/skolem/9f2c> ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid asserting it by hand on a demonstrand (leaving it UNasserted is exactly what forces the chase to invent the witness) and avoid pointing it at an ordinary domain individual instead of a logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf — it is the existential head whose obligation the chase discharges."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Leave it UNasserted on the seeded demonstrand individuals and let the native existential chase materialize it against a freshly invented Skolem witness; read the reasoned edge to walk from a demonstrand to the gmeow:InventedWitness the chase minted for it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the existential head property of the demonstrator's C ⊑ ∃p.D law — the edge the native chase materializes to a chase-invented Skolem witness."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf
    a logic:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Chase Witness Leaf"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The narrow, plain leaf class the invented Skolem witness of a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand inhabits — the `D` in the demonstrator's C ⊑ ∃p.D law. It is deliberately a LEAF: it carries no existential obligation of its own, no OWL disjointWith, and no functional or cardinality axiom, and it does NOT reach logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand, so a chase-invented null typed into it triggers no further inference, no Skolem ancestor-blocking cycle, and no global inconsistency. Its whole role is to be the harmless target type the ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf obligation is satisfied against, keeping the demonstrator weakly-acyclic and terminating."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/skolem/9f2c> a logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid giving it any existential obligation, OWL disjointWith, or functional/cardinality axiom, and avoid letting it reach logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand — a self-referential or disjointness-bearing witness leaf turns the demonstrator's invented null into a provenance cycle or a global inconsistency."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Use it only as the plain target type of the demonstrator's existential obligation; keep it a sink — no subclass axioms, no disjointness — so the chase-invented witness typed into it stays inert."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the harmless leaf type a chase-invented Skolem witness inhabits when the native existential chase discharges the demonstrator's C ⊑ ∃p.D obligation."@x-gmeow-english .

logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "existential chase demonstrand alpha"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The first seeded demonstrand of the native existential chase: a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand asserted with NO logic:demonstratesChaseWitness edge, so the chase must invent a fresh Skolem witness (a gmeow:InventedWitness) to satisfy its ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf obligation. Paired with logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandBeta so the chase mints two DISTINCT nulls, one per instance, in the same world."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandBeta
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "existential chase demonstrand beta"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The second seeded demonstrand of the native existential chase: a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand asserted with NO logic:demonstratesChaseWitness edge, so the chase must invent a fresh Skolem witness (a gmeow:InventedWitness) to satisfy its ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf obligation. Paired with logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha so the chase mints two DISTINCT nulls, one per instance, in the same world."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The graph-box role partition — description-logic knowledge-base partitioning.
#
# TBox / RBox / ABox is the description-logic partition of a knowledge base
# into terminology, role behaviour, and assertions; CBox and ConfigBox extend
# it to statement context and operational configuration. That subject matter is
# a LOGICAL FORMALISM, so docs/GROUNDING.md's "External grounding ownership"
# table places it in the logical grounding domain and its tier rule fixes the
# reconciliation direction: `logic:` owns the concept and every other slice
# consumes it. The cluster — the gmeow:GraphBoxRole value type, its five role
# individuals, and the gmeow:graphBoxRole property that attaches them — moves
# as ONE unit, because splitting a value type from its property across a
# grounding and a non-grounding slice is the very split the rule forbids.
#
# Each term carries gmeow:groundingConceptDomain gmeow:groundingDomainLogical:
# the authored judgment that its subject matter is logical, which is what the
# slice-ownership.grounding-downward-dependency gate reads. Ownership is by
# rdfs:isDefinedBy and physical module, so the IRIs stay in the gmeow:
# namespace and not one referencing triple anywhere in the corpus changes.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

gmeow:GraphBoxRole
    a logic:AbstractIndividualType ,
        logic:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "Graph Box Role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    skos:definition "A documentation and validation role describing which graph layer a term, shape, module, or graph artifact primarily serves: assertional data (ABox), terminology/schema (TBox), role/property behavior (RBox), contextual statement metadata (CBox), or runtime/package/profile configuration (ConfigBox). Roles are descriptive annotations, may be multi-valued, and never partition the ontology into exactly one box per resource."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:confidence gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxCBox ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using box roles as logical class membership, named-graph routing, or an exactly-one partition; a construct can legitimately serve more than one box."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:groundingConceptDomain gmeow:groundingDomainLogical ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Annotate the subject with one or more gmeow:graphBoxRole values. Tooling may render the roles in describe output, generated docs, validation reports, and GTS/package summaries, but the annotations do not alter OWL entailments."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when a term, shape, generated report, or documentation surface needs to say whether it is about asserted data, schema/logic, role/property behavior, statement context, or operational configuration/profile metadata."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:boxABox
    a gmeow:GraphBoxRole ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ABox role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Assertional graph role: concrete instance data, examples, claims, and payload triples that are validated, transported, projected, or reasoned over by GMEOW tooling."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A slice example graph or a user's imported data graph is ABox-role content."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid for term definitions, class/property axioms, and shape declarations unless those resources are themselves being treated as data."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:groundingConceptDomain gmeow:groundingDomainLogical ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Annotate examples, payload graph descriptors, and validation report context with this role when users need to see that a diagnostic came from asserted data."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for resources that primarily describe asserted instance content rather than the schema that constrains it."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:boxCBox
    a gmeow:GraphBoxRole ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "CBox role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Contextual graph role: metadata about assertions, especially RDF 1.2 reifiers and statement annotations carrying provenance, evidence, confidence, temporal scope, standpoint, determinacy, validity, or disclosure context."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A reifier that records confidence and evidence for an assertion is CBox-role data."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid for deployment configuration or package-profile metadata unless it is explicitly contextual metadata about an assertion; use gmeow:boxConfigBox for operational configuration."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:groundingConceptDomain gmeow:groundingDomainLogical ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Annotate statement-metadata terms and reifier-focused SHACL shapes so validation can surface contextual assertion failures as CBox diagnostics."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for statement context and assertion envelopes, especially when a shape or report is validating metadata attached to a reified statement."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:boxConfigBox
    a gmeow:GraphBoxRole ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "ConfigBox role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Configuration graph role: runtime, package, profile, solver, deployment, service-description, and transport metadata that controls how GMEOW artifacts are built, selected, bundled, served, or consumed, without being statement-context metadata about a particular assertion."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A GTS profile or service-description term that configures an offline package carries the ConfigBox role."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid for provenance, evidence, confidence, standpoint, disclosure, or validity metadata attached to a particular assertion; those are CBox concerns."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:groundingConceptDomain gmeow:groundingDomainLogical ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Annotate configuration and profile surfaces so docs, exports, validation reports, and package summaries can distinguish operational configuration from assertion context."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for configuration/profile terms and graph artifacts that describe how tooling, packages, services, solvers, transports, or deployment surfaces should operate."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:boxRBox
    a gmeow:GraphBoxRole ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "RBox role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Role/property graph role: property axioms and relationship behavior, including inverses, transitivity, property chains, disjointness, path behavior, and role-like constraints over predicates."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:partOf carries the RBox role because it is a transitive role/property spine."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it for every object property automatically when the property is merely a simple data slot and no role behavior is being documented."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:groundingConceptDomain gmeow:groundingDomainLogical ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Annotate relationship spines, generated path constraints, and property-behavior documentation so reports can identify RBox failures without reverse-engineering the shape IRI."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for properties, path shapes, and role-behavior declarations where the important diagnostic context is the predicate or relation itself."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:boxTBox
    a gmeow:GraphBoxRole ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "TBox role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Terminological graph role: classes, datatypes, shapes, profiles, restrictions, logic-profile declarations, and other schema or vocabulary constructs that describe how assertions are structured."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:GraphBoxRole and a SHACL node shape both carry the TBox role."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid for ordinary instance claims unless the claim is explicitly about schema or vocabulary resources."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:groundingConceptDomain gmeow:groundingDomainLogical ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Annotate schema-bearing resources so docs and validation output can identify vocabulary/shape problems separately from data and statement-context problems."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for terms, shapes, modules, and profile declarations that define the vocabulary or constraints used by data."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:graphBoxRole
    a logic:AnnotationProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    rdfs:label "graph box role"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:GraphBoxRole ;
    skos:definition "Links a term, shape, module, graph artifact, or validation result source to one or more gmeow:GraphBoxRole individuals. The role is advisory metadata for documentation, validation diagnostics, and package consumers; it carries no OWL logical semantics."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:partOf gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating it as an ownership, import, or named-graph directive; the canonical source/projection rules still decide where data is authored and generated."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:groundingConceptDomain gmeow:groundingDomainLogical ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Attach one or more role individuals such as gmeow:boxTBox, gmeow:boxCBox, or gmeow:boxConfigBox. Consumers should preserve unknown future roles and must not assume the value set is closed."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to make a construct's graph-layer role explicit for readers and tools, especially when validation output needs to distinguish data, schema, role/property, and statement-context failures."@x-gmeow-english .
